sequenceDiagram
    title Target MySQL-only hotel search - issue 153
    autonumber
    participant Web as Vue guest client
    participant API as Search controller
    participant Search as Search application
    participant Repo as Repositories
    participant DB as Local MySQL
    participant Redis as Redis history
    participant Events as Publisher / NATS

    opt User types a destination
        Web->>API: GET /search/destinations/autocomplete
        API->>Search: Normalize text and aliases
        Search->>Repo: Find active matching destinations
        Repo->>DB: Read destinations
        DB-->>Repo: Destination candidates
        Repo-->>Search: Matching names and IDs
        Search->>Search: Rank exact, prefix, substring and typo suggestions
        Search-->>API: Suggestions
        API-->>Web: 200 suggestions with destination IDs
    end

    Web->>Web: Submit dates and guests, update Router and Vuex
    opt New base criteria, preserving current client logging behavior
        Web->>Web: Save browser recent-search history
        Web->>API: POST /search/log
        API->>Events: Publish search-performed event, best effort
        Events-->>API: Publish attempt completed
        API-->>Web: 201 log response
    end

    Web->>API: GET /search/hotels with criteria, filters and page
    API->>API: Optional authentication and Joi validation
    API->>Search: searchHotels(params, userId)
    Search->>Repo: Resolve active destination by ID or normalized text
    Repo->>DB: Query destinations
    DB-->>Repo: Destination or unresolved text intent
    Repo-->>Search: Resolved search intent

    Search->>Repo: Search eligible hotel offers in batch
    Repo->>DB: Filter hotel candidates by location, text and static criteria
    DB->>DB: Aggregate daily inventory by room type for all stay nights
    DB->>DB: Check rooms and occupancy, subtract bookings and holds
    DB->>DB: Price eligible offers, apply budget and cancellation rules
    DB->>DB: Select cheapest qualifying offer per hotel
    DB-->>Repo: Eligible hotel-offer rows
    Repo-->>Search: Full eligible set without per-hotel query fan-out

    alt Eligible hotels exist
        Search->>Search: Score review quality, popularity and optional distance
        Search->>Search: Build facets and total, apply requested sort and pagination
        opt Authenticated user
            Search->>Repo: Fetch favorite IDs for the displayed page
            Repo->>DB: Batch favorite lookup
            DB-->>Repo: Favorite hotel IDs
            Repo-->>Search: Favorite IDs
        end
        Search->>Search: Format page, offers, coordinates and metadata
    else No eligible hotels
        Search->>Search: Format successful empty results and facets
    end

    Search-->>API: Search response and resolved destination
    opt Authenticated user
        API-)Redis: Record recent search, not awaited
    end
    API-)Events: Publish search-performed event, not awaited
    API-->>Web: 200 hotels, pagination, facets and metadata
    Web->>Web: Render hotel cards, map data or empty state

    Note over Repo,DB: SQL stages are logical steps of a bounded set-based query plan, not one query per hotel.
    Note over Search,DB: One room type per offer. Search does not reserve rooms. Booking rechecks inventory atomically.
    Note over Events: Go analytics consumes NATS events and writes MongoDB independently of the search response.
